<!-- Raku overrides for the Default scheme.

     Deliberately tiny. Every RAKU_* key falls back to a platform key (see
     RakuHighlighter.kt), so Raku inherits whatever colors the active scheme
     already defines for operators, variables, types and the rest. This file
     used to restate ~37 of those as hardcoded foregrounds, which meant Raku
     looked one way under Default/Darcula and another under every third-party
     theme, which only ever saw the fallbacks.

     What is left encodes something no platform key can express. Add an entry
     here only when that is true; otherwise change the key's fallback. -->
<list>
  <!-- Pod B<> and I<> used to live here as FONT_TYPE entries. They are gone:
       an entry in this file is only seen by schemes derived from this one, so
       under a third-party theme B<> fell through to DOC_COMMENT and rendered
       in the doc-comment color and not bold. They are now drawn by layering
       RakuHighlighter.Style.BOLD / .ITALIC, whose font style is the key's own
       default and so applies under every scheme.

       U<> was never here. An underline needs an EFFECT_COLOR, and naming one
       would take the key out of the fallback path entirely, so it is resolved
       from the active theme at apply time; see
       RakuHighlighter.StyleEffect. RAKU_REGEX_SIG_SPACE likewise. -->
  <!-- The whole point of ALT_WARNING is to be distinguishable from an
       ordinary weak warning, which its WEAK_WARNING_ATTRIBUTES fallback
       would make it identical to.
       TODO: Match this up with the genuine blue from the default scheme -->
  <option name="RAKU_ALT_WARNING">
    <value>
      <option name="EFFECT_COLOR" value="56A8F5" />
      <option name="ERROR_STRIPE_COLOR" value="56A8F5" />
      <option name="EFFECT_TYPE" value="2" />
    </value>
  </option>
</list>
